From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ppe_ds: default to polling mode

The PPE-DS index synchronisation runs either from a hrtimer (polling) or from
a pair of interrupts.  Interrupt mode needs the WLAN driver to register a
PPEDS interrupt and to implement the tx-consume-intr callback, which ath12k
only does through QSDK's private hif helpers -- the mainline ath12k has no
such thing, so in interrupt mode nobody ever reports "WLAN consumed the
descriptors", nss-ppe waits for that event forever and the Direct Switch
stops after the first ring wrap.

Default to polling mode (hrtimer, IDX_MGMT_PERIOD is derived from the
idx_mgmt_freq module parameter) so that the index sync works with the
callbacks ath12k already provides.  It can still be overridden at load time
with qca-nss-ppe-ds.polling_for_idx_update=0 once the interrupt path exists.

--- a/drv/ppe_ds/ppe_ds_main.c
+++ b/drv/ppe_ds/ppe_ds_main.c
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
  * and PPE_DS_POLL_MODE (1) will use polling mode.
  *
  */
-unsigned int polling_for_idx_update = PPE_DS_INTR_MODE;
+unsigned int polling_for_idx_update = PPE_DS_POLL_MODE;
 module_param(polling_for_idx_update,
 		uint, S_IRUSR | S_IWUSR | S_IRGRP | S_IROTH);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(polling_for_idx_update, "Enable/Disable PPE DS poll mode");
